(ROADMAP M0 — dynamic buffer growth. A dynamic buffer starts small and must
 grow as content is appended; a fixed-size buffer must NOT grow, and a write
 past its end is a no-op that sets the error flag. Both halves are asserted
 here because README's memory model now states both, and the two behaviours
 were documented inconsistently until they were reconciled.)

Create a buffer called "grower".
a number called "i" is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 500,
  Append "0123456789" to grower,
  Increment i.
print grower's size.

a buffer called "fixed" is 4 bytes in size.
Set byte 100 of fixed to 65.
on error print "fixed buffer refused the out-of-bounds write".
Set byte 1 of fixed to 65.
Set byte 2 of fixed to 66.
print fixed.
